    "senderName": "NWS Tiyan GU",
    "headline": "Rip Current Statement issued November 28 at 2:54PM ChST until December 3 at 4:00PM ChST by NWS Tiyan GU",
    "description": "* WHAT...Dangerous rip currents.\n\n* WHERE...East facing reefs of the Marianas.\n\n* WHEN...Through Thursday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Rip currents can sweep even the best swimmers away\nfrom shore into deeper water.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Surging trade winds will continue to\nproduce elevated trade-wind swell, leading to elevated surf and a\nhigh risk of rip currents along east-facing reefs for much of the\nweek, through at least Thursday afternoon.",
    "instruction": "Rip currents will be life threatening. If caught in a rip\ncurrent, relax and float. Don't swim against the current. If\nable, swim in a direction following the shoreline. If unable to\nescape, face the shore and call or wave for help.",
    "response": "Avoid",
